{"title":"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Trig_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Trig Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The inscribed circle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent\" title=\"Tangent\">tangent</a> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72372ce518e97b2d43a1f0bcafbdc88302ed9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" />  and its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2dcca7072789631c895ee0608a4335ae85faa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=23$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cb7944dd4e97e4a590671ff60c8b6f273ab6d08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB=27,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> find the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> of the triangle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd1d3a517ae3f4ddc9470481bb6e69b4808fbfaf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pathpen = black + linewidth(0.65); pointpen = black; pair A=(0,0),B=(50,0),C=IP(circle(A,23+245/2),circle(B,27+245/2)), I=incenter(A,B,C); path P = incircle(A,B,C); D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A)--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,N)--cycle);D(P); D(MP(&quot;P&quot;,IP(A--B,P))); pair Q=IP(C--A,P),R=IP(B--C,P); D(MP(&quot;R&quot;,R,NE));D(MP(&quot;Q&quot;,Q,NW)); MP(&quot;23&quot;,(A+Q)/2,W);MP(&quot;27&quot;,(B+R)/2,E); [/asy]\" width=\"118\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the tangency point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem\" title=\"Two Tangent Theorem\">Two Tangent Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e16a16a5e03586d6d86505be10828e67ce57b0e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = AQ = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98bb4183e801c154d960c1ffe9f11f74ba9a1db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = BR = 27$\" width=\"124\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f609684f0af459721a835304e129308aed69135.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CQ = CR = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e5247650c5040309690323b27391e1a96792eed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs = A$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d2daae9c005b2b8d11cb4f1991e4a3fc70d2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{27 \\cdot 2 + 23 \\cdot 2 + x \\cdot 2}{2} = 50 + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"269\" height=\"37\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c435934904921e25052717b780d6f19fd4a13c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(21)(50 + x) = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Heron%27s_formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Heron&#39;s formula\">Heron's formula</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d78f441ff3e49aa8e282ebfed87db4dc2f7bcb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} = \\sqrt{(50+x)(x)(23)(27)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"420\" height=\"32\" />. Equating and squaring both sides, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/384ebeab318f9bebe5275a899c6ed2423f1cb2f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}  [21(50+x)]^2 &amp;=&amp; (50+x)(x)(621)\\\\ 441(50+x) &amp;=&amp; 621x\\\\ 180x = 441 \\cdot 50 &amp;\\Longrightarrow &amp; x = \\frac{245}{2}   \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"310\" height=\"87\" />\n</p><p>We want the perimeter, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/7/5d7960bcec8ad37fa462b46f454054011738e5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2s = 2\\left(50 + \\frac{245}{2}\\right) = \\boxed{345}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"215\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the incenter be denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  It is commonly known that the incenter is the intersection of the angle bisectors of a triangle.  So let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c6640e59b52a50efc7db91a73baa297eabffc95b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABI = \\angle CBI = \\alpha, \\angle BAI = \\angle CAI = \\beta,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"334\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e89ed23e399e76e9b3315a62f55bf9f903269c29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCI = \\angle ACI = \\gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f320cc86147d3a68e8f96f832495a4d8907a542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\tan \\alpha &amp; = &amp; \\frac {21}{27} \\\\ \\tan \\beta &amp; = &amp; \\frac {21}{23} \\\\ \\tan \\gamma &amp; = &amp; \\frac {21}x. \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"114\" height=\"123\" />\nSo naturally we look at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a18a1df56f2f7982c3e9d9f1eb3d7f7136e67bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />  But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c94c819e6625567616cbc4ad072bb271ff6b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma = \\frac \\pi2 - (\\beta + \\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"129\" height=\"33\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/4447a4274423fef766267d2195c0c998566964e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\tan \\gamma &amp; = &amp; \\tan\\left(\\frac \\pi2 - (\\beta + \\alpha)\\right) \\\\ &amp; = &amp; \\frac 1{\\tan(\\alpha + \\beta)} \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\frac {21}x &amp; = &amp; \\frac {1 - \\frac {21\\cdot 21}{23\\cdot 27}}{\\frac {21}{27} + \\frac {21}{23}} \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"235\" height=\"134\" />\nDoing the algebra, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e59556448d5a406a4b679b9b05c741c9201400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac {245}2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The perimeter is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62d5015c54c85c139fd2f4103ad14f9b0980c06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot\\frac {245}2 + 2\\cdot 23 + 2\\cdot 27 = \\boxed{345}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"248\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let unknown side has length as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, Assume three sides of triangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11e5bfef7ef06a2d05b69a39423fc9ae8f8657a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{2S}{a+b+c}=21,S=1050+21x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"283\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/68295a16bfa282f8bf6b6b794e4773fea5c12f6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\angle{\\frac{B}{2}}=\\frac{7}{9}, \\tan\\angle{B}=\\frac{63}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"211\" height=\"39\" />. Use trig identity, knowing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e65f27d2807e1d932c1c2c57b138602a952b339.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\cot^2\\angle{B}=\\csc^2\\angle{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />, getting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6438c0df5948c634a7f8108b946f627fb8173c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\angle{B}=\\frac{63}{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8359995e00844cba24b259b195855f4052244b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+27)*50*\\frac{63}{65}*\\frac{1}{2}=1050+21x; x=\\frac{245}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"357\" height=\"38\" />, the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d78223e4e8e8d81732cc6c5a24502f1dab2748e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$245+100=345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />\n~bluesoul\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Trig_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Trig_Bash)\">Solution 4 (Trig Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Trig Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545620eea637fd3eca1c0b2cb97f9911aff2ed4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.65); pointpen = black; pair A=(0,0), B=(50,0); pair C=IP(circle(A,23+245/2),circle(B,27+245/2)); pair O = incenter(A,B,C);  path P_circle = incircle(A,B,C); pair P = foot(O, A, B); pair Q = foot(O, A, C); pair R = foot(O, B, C); D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A, SW)--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B, SE)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,N)--cycle); D(P_circle); D(O--B, dashed + blue); D(O--P, blue); dot(MP(&quot;O&quot;, O, NW)); D(MP(&quot;P&quot;, P, S)); D(MP(&quot;R&quot;, R, NE)); D(MP(&quot;Q&quot;, Q, NW)); MP(&quot;23&quot;, (A+P)/2, S); MP(&quot;27&quot;, (B+P)/2, S); MP(&quot;23&quot;, (A+Q)/2, W); MP(&quot;27&quot;, (B+R)/2, E); MP(&quot;x&quot;, (C+R)/2, NE); MP(&quot;x&quot;, (C+Q)/2, NW); D(rightanglemark(O,P,B, 1.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"118\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>Let \\(CR = CQ = x\\). Using the inradius formula for the area of a triangle, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6a11d49ae45af2d279bce7aeda12e00531265e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC] = 1050 + 21x,\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere \\([ABC]\\) denotes the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\).\n</p><p>Next, we find \\(\\sin \\angle CBA\\). Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4acfc5749b41e48cefa2e816ab79f381a2a3ac05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CBA = \\angle RBP = 2\\angle OBP.\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>First, we find the hypotenuse \\(OB\\) using the Pythagorean Theorem:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb88ade3862917d756582d009e1ce34e8a710ca5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OB^2 = 27^2 + 21^2 = 1170 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad OB = 3\\sqrt{130}.\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let \\(\\angle OBP = \\theta\\). Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae03d0f9904d3fe52e9aa2ad9b09b65733b1af81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\theta = \\frac{21}{3\\sqrt{130}}, \\qquad \\cos \\theta = \\frac{27}{3\\sqrt{130}}.\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Using the double-angle identity,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9ed3393c83220c2d1ca87841993647506e32eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(2\\theta) = 2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta= 2\\left(\\frac{21}{3\\sqrt{130}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{27}{3\\sqrt{130}}\\right)= \\frac{1134}{1170}= \\frac{63}{65}.\\]\" width=\"481\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now we compute the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) using the formula \\(\\tfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/7/a67b65e49bbb3a10920513fbf86251973f9eb8f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC] = \\frac{1}{2}(50)(27+x)\\left(\\frac{63}{65}\\right)= \\frac{315}{13}(27+x).\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Equating the two expressions for the area,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebaf34dd42c893fd73ef5bcc881d11bec8196ccb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1050 + 21x = \\frac{315}{13}(27+x).\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Solving,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/f/f1fa11be09973fc1ee72ea1c12efad61c6a88c9f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{13}{15}x + \\frac{130}{3} = 27 + x,\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"37\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543990a0d5799cc53d8bd962274b2d73e3cce53d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{49}{3} = \\frac{2}{15}x,\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"37\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f9d52244eb17cb8193f08116062c002b353ba0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{245}{2}.\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Finally, we compute the perimeter of \\(\\triangle ABC\\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12ecd8510329a47b51d904953506905bf85225e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(23+27) + 2\\left(\\frac{245}{2}\\right) = \\boxed{345}.\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~Voidling\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME\" title=\"1999 AIME\">1999 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" tit